# Secrets
*key*
*.pem
*.env
# `*.env` only matches names ENDING in .env, so it never matched the timestamped
# copies a helper wrote next to it: .env.bak-20260805-222102 and
# .env.bak2-20260805-222324 were committed by auto-push.sh in 6ed5d40 and pushed
# to origin/main with 26 live values in them (ANTHROPIC/OPENAI/DEEPSEEK/GEMINI/
# EXA/MINIMAX keys, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET, RSI_SIGNING_KEY).
# A secrets pattern that only covers the exact filename is not a secrets pattern.
.env*
# Same class: timestamped throwaway backups. auto-push.sh does a bare `git commit`
# of everything staged, so any *.bak a script drops beside a config becomes
# permanent history — nine of them already are.
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
# ...and the plain form. `config.yaml.corrupt.20260617-135424.bak` ends in a bare
# `.bak`, so neither pattern above matched it — and a history sweep of all 11,678
# blobs found it still TRACKED and on disk holding the same DEEPSEEK_API_KEY that
# is live in .env today. Three near-miss patterns for one class of file is the tell
# that the pattern list is the wrong control; see the content guard in auto-push.sh.
*.bak
auth.json
auth.lock
gateway*
processes.json

# Runtime data
state.db*
kanban.db*
cache/
logs/
audio_cache/
image_cache/
sandboxes/
cron/output/

# Atomic-write scratch from the cron scheduler. jobs.py:557 does
# mkstemp(dir=cron/, prefix='.jobs_', suffix='.tmp') -> fsync -> atomic_replace(:563),
# and suggestions.py:92 does the same with prefix '.sugg_'. The temp file exists for
# the few ms between mkstemp and the rename.
#
# That window is not a rare one to hit: `git add -A` enumerates cron/ and then stats
# each entry to stage it, and the scheduler rewrites jobs.json to record last_run_at
# for the very job running auto-push.sh — so the writer and the reader are guaranteed
# to overlap. The rename lands between readdir and stat and git aborts the WHOLE sync:
#   fatal: unable to stat 'cron/.jobs_119c4ssq.tmp': No such file or directory
# (21:01 on 2026-08-14; the run pushed nothing). Ignored entries are skipped during
# traversal and never stat'd, which closes the race — measured at 4/5 runs failing
# without these two lines and 0/4 with them, in scripts/test_auto_push_tmp_race.sh.
#
# cron/output/.output_*.tmp (jobs.py:1243) is already covered by cron/output/ above.
cron/.jobs_*.tmp
cron/.sugg_*.tmp

# Daemon-written runtime churn — was the GIT_DIRTY noise source (war-room 2026-06-20).
# Versioning these made the watchdog's GIT_DIRTY detector fire on every relay/metric write,
# burying real source signal. They are derived/runtime; the workload owns them, not git.
queue/
meta/
state/
sessions/
.update_check
models_dev_cache.json
# Same class: provider model lists the brain picker refetches on a fingerprint miss.
provider_models_cache.json
ollama_cloud_models_cache.json
# Runtime dedup state the inbound adapter rewrites on every poll.
feishu_seen_message_ids.json

# Python bytecode (derived)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store
models/*.onnx
models/miniLM-onnx/onnx/

# Live SQLite databases — never versioned. git add -A used to sweep coordinator.db (29MB,
# 75 commits) and its -wal (121 commits); a WAL-mode file copied mid-write is a torn
# snapshot anyway. backups/coordinator.db.latest.gz is the consistent copy that IS tracked,
# so these patterns are anchored to the repo root and do not match it.
/coordinator.db*
/sessions.db*
/scripts/coordinator.db*
/*.db-shm
/*.db-wal

# Timestamped rolling snapshots from db_health.py (it keeps the last 7 on disk).
# state-*.db.gz is ~36MB each, so auto-push.sh's 5MB backstop refused them every hour
# and its stderr was nothing but those refusals from 2026-08-02 onward. Deliberately
# NOT anchored to backups/coordinator.db.latest.gz — the dot-form name above is the
# consistent copy that IS tracked, and neither pattern here matches it.
backups/coordinator-*.db.gz
backups/state-*.db.gz

# 72MB whole-repo dump produced by repomix for one-off LLM context. Regenerable,
# never a source of truth.
repomix-output.xml

# Regenerable skills-hub index cache (built by tools/skills_hub.py). At 39MB it trips
# auto-push.sh's 5MB backstop every hour with no human action possible to silence it.
/skills/.hub/index-cache/

backups/state-*.db

# Staged into the build context by deploy/hermes/deploy.sh, never committed.
vendor/
